  "summary": "All checks pass (lint clean, build OK, 145 tests green).\n\nI read the four items as a conformance check against the existing screens and only changed what was not already true here.\n\n**Changed:**\n- **UC8 — matched word highlighting.** Added `src/features/contract-repository/components/HighlightedText.jsx` (case-insensitive, regex-escaped) and wired it into `ContractListTable.jsx` for contract name, counterparty, value, start/end date and owner; `ContractRepositoryPage.jsx` now passes the active `filters.searchText` down.\n- **UC10 — \"the user picks Excel or PDF\".** `TrackerExportButton.jsx` now renders a format select (Excel / PDF) next to the Export button and passes the chosen format to `onExport`; `TrackerPage.jsx` stopped hard-coding `'Excel'` and passes `handleExport` directly, so the export request carries the picked format alongside the current tab, period and filters it already sent.\n\n**Already true, left alone:** UC7 provider-connection failure (`SignerListPage.jsx` shows \"Unable to connect to the selected e-signature provider…\" on `SignatureConnectionFailed` with no status change), the Executed state / audit-certificate download after the last signature, UC8's \"No contracts found matching your search.\" message, all of UC9 (empty message, \"AI Suggested\" badge, Accept/Edit), and UC10's \"Export failed. Please try again.\" in-place failure message.\n\nPDF locking, audit-certificate generation, obligation extraction on Executed, and the actual export file content are backend behaviours in the separate API repository — I did not stub them here; the frontend only consumes their responses.",
